s_error":false,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I reviewed PKT-0018 and am approving it. The other agent's numbers back its conclusion, and every gap it leaves is admitted and handed to a follow-up request.\n\n- **Goal:** all three parts are done.\n  - **Delay breakdown:** the server's share stays at or under 69 ms at the 99th percentile and doesn't grow with more clients. The 4-client delay sits on the browser side: 1.8 s between keystroke and send, 0.9 s before the receiver picks the message up, while the machine was about 99% busy. So \"the browsers are short of CPU\" is supported by the data, not just guessed.\n  - **Load test:** it went up to 100 documents × 10 clients.\n  - **Large files:** opening and conversion were measured on large files. Saving was only approximated, by timing the conversion a save performs (\"service → own format\" column). Real saves under load all failed, and the log says so instead of hiding it.\n- **Contract:** no project source changed. The only change outside the measurement files is the DocService logging setting, which is config.\n- **Budget:** counting `baseline.md`, the four scripts and the results JSON gives 6 files, which is the limit. That assumes the packet file, friction entry and spawn request don't count toward it. The factory's scope check passed. About 490 changed lines against a limit of 800.\n- **Being honest about results:** three problems are recorded rather than smoothed over: the 200 × 5 run that never finished, saves failing with callback status 3, and the one 124 s pptx → pdf conversion. The baseline marks the save timings as indicative only. The gaps table now points at the new follow-up instead of the old one.\n- **Rejection rules (TEP-0004):** the executor log is filled in. The \"Spawned packets\" section is empty, but the follow-up request is in `.theseus/spawn/PKT-0018-load-test-beyond-1000-sockets-valid-saves-under.md` and covers all three open items. This is an investigate packet, so the rule about keeping surprises in tests doesn't apply.\n- **Small weaknesses, not blocking:**\n  - The acceptance check `test -s` passes before any work is done; the friction entry already says so.\n  - The 124 s outlier is one in three runs, so its p50 means little.\n  - Calling 768 connections \"nginx's default\" is plausible, but the executor gives no config excerpt showing that value.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE goal met with data that supports it, contract respected, gaps recorded and follow-up requested in .theseus/spawn/","ttft_ms":2175,"type":"result","duration_ms":16904,"uuid":"662f6e08-9852-4958-ab51-ecf9247f74ff","ttft_stream_ms":859,"time_to_request_ms":283,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":153,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":25,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":23,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":47,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":174,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":217,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":141,"process_rss_mib_result":229,"process_anon_mib_result":139,"process_peak_rss_mib":261,"process_cpu_ms_turn":950,"process_wall_ms_turn":16904,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":424,"process_wall_ms_streaming":14148,"main_stream_count":4,"main_stream_event_count":259,"main_stream_chunk_count":78,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":7,"cpu_ms":22,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":8,"ambient_wait_ms":6,"render_ms":1,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":859,"time_to_request_fro